#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/fsmount.2:23
msgid ""
"The B<fsmount>()  system call is part of the suite of file-descriptor-based "
"mount facilities in Linux."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/fsmount.2:37
msgid ""
"B<fsmount>()  creates a new detached mount object for the root of the new "
"filesystem instance referenced by the filesystem context file descriptor "
"I<fsfd>.  A new file descriptor associated with the detached mount object is "
"then returned.  In order to create a mount object with B<fsmount>(), the "
"calling process must have the B<\\%CAP_SYS_ADMIN> capability."
msgstr ""

#.  FS_CONTEXT_AWAITING_MOUNT is the term the kernel uses for this.
#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/fsmount.2:58
msgid ""
"The filesystem context must have been created with a call to B<fsopen>(2)  "
"and then had a filesystem instance instantiated with a call to "
"B<fsconfig>(2)  with B<\\%FSCONFIG_CMD_CREATE> or B<\\"
"%FSCONFIG_CMD_CREATE_EXCL> in order to be in the correct state for this "
"operation (the \"awaiting-mount\" mode in kernel-developer parlance).  "
"Unlike B<open_tree>(2)  with B<\\%OPEN_TREE_CLONE>, B<fsmount>()  can only "
"be called once in the lifetime of a filesystem context to produce a mount "
"object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/fsmount.2:93
msgid ""
"As with file descriptors returned from B<open_tree>(2)  called with "
"B<OPEN_TREE_CLONE>, the returned file descriptor can then be used with "
"B<move_mount>(2), B<mount_setattr>(2), or other such system calls to do "
"further mount operations.  This mount object will be unmounted and destroyed "
"when the file descriptor is closed if it was not otherwise attached to a "
"mount point by calling B<move_mount>(2).  (Note that the unmount operation "
"on B<close>(2)  is lazy\\[em]akin to calling B<umount2>(2)  with "
"B<MNT_DETACH>; any existing open references to files from the mount object "
"will continue to work, and the mount object will only be completely "
"destroyed once it ceases to be busy.)  The returned file descriptor also "
"acts the same as one produced by B<open>(2)  with B<O_PATH>, meaning it can "
"also be used as a I<dirfd> argument to \"*at()\" system calls."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/fsmount.2:100
msgid ""
"I<flags> controls the creation of the returned file descriptor.  A value for "
"I<flags> is constructed by bitwise ORing zero or more of the following "
"constants:"
msgstr ""

