"I<from_dirfd> and I<from_path> on top of the mount stack, attach or move it "
"beneath the current top mount on the mount stack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:284
msgid ""
"After using B<\\%MOVE_MOUNT_BENEATH>, it is possible to B<umount>(2)  the "
"top mount in order to reveal the mount object which was attached beneath it "
"earlier.  This allows for the seamless (and atomic) replacement of intricate "
"mount trees, which can further be used to \"upgrade\" a mount tree with a "
"newer version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:286
msgid "This operation has several restrictions:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:297
msgid ""
"Mount objects cannot be attached beneath the filesystem root, including "
"cases where the filesystem root was configured by B<chroot>(2)  or "
"B<pivot_root>(2).  To mount beneath the filesystem root, B<pivot_root>(2)  "
"must be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:309
msgid ""
"The target path indicated by I<to_dirfd> and I<to_path> must not be a "
"detached mount object, such as those produced by B<open_tree>(2)  with B<\\"
"%OPEN_TREE_CLONE> or B<fsmount>(2)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:314
msgid ""
"The current top mount of the target path's mount stack and its parent mount "
"must be in the calling process's mount namespace."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:320
msgid ""
"The caller must have sufficient privileges to unmount the top mount of the "
"target path's mount stack, to prove they have privileges to reveal the "
"underlying mount."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:329
msgid ""
"Mount propagation events triggered by this B<move_mount>()  operation (as "
"described in B<mount_namespaces>(7))  are calculated based on the parent "
"mount of the current top mount of the target path's mount stack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:333
msgid ""
"The target path's mount cannot be an ancestor in the mount tree of the "
"source mount object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:338
msgid ""
"The source mount object must not have any overmounts, otherwise it would be "
"possible to create \"shadow mounts\" (i.e., two mounts mounted on the same "
"parent mount at the same mount point)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:352
msgid ""
"It is not possible to move a mount beneath a top mount if the parent mount "
"of the current top mount propagates to the top mount itself.  Otherwise, B<\\"
"%MOVE_MOUNT_BENEATH> would cause the mount object to be propagated to the "
"top mount from the parent mount, defeating the purpose of using B<\\"
"%MOVE_MOUNT_BENEATH>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:363
msgid ""
"It is not possible to move a mount beneath a top mount if the parent mount "
"of the current top mount propagates to the mount object being mounted "
"beneath.  Otherwise, this would cause a similar propagation issue to the "
"previous point, also defeating the purpose of using B<\\%MOVE_MOUNT_BENEATH>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:381
msgid ""
"If I<from_dirfd> is a mount object file descriptor and B<move_mount>()  is "
"operating on it directly, I<from_dirfd> will remain associated with the "
"mount object after B<move_mount>()  succeeds, so you may repeatedly use "
"I<from_dirfd> with B<move_mount>(2)  and/or \"*at()\" system calls as many "
"times as necessary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/move_mount.2:388
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "On success, zero is returned.  On error, -1 is returned, and I<errno> is "
#| "set appropriately."
