#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:516
msgid ""
"The bind-mount mount objects created by B<open_tree>()  with B<\\"
"%OPEN_TREE_CLONE> are not associated with the mount namespace of the calling "
"process.  Instead, each mount object is placed in a newly allocated "
"\"anonymous\" mount namespace associated with the calling process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:537
msgid ""
"One of the side-effects of this is that (unlike bind-mounts created with "
"B<mount>(2)), mount propagation (as described in B<mount_namespaces>(7))  "
"will not be applied to bind-mounts created by B<open_tree>()  until the bind-"
"mount is attached with B<move_mount>(2), at which point the mount object "
"will be associated with the mount namespace where it was attached and mount "
"propagation will resume.  Note that any mount propagation events that "
"occurred before the mount object was attached will I<not> be propagated to "
"the mount object, even after it is attached."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:544
msgid ""
"The following examples show how B<open_tree>()  can be used in place of more "
"traditional B<mount>(2)  calls with B<MS_BIND>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:549
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int srcfd = open_tree(AT_FDCWD, \"/var\", OPEN_TREE_CLONE);\n"
"move_mount(srcfd, \"\", AT_FDCWD, \"/mnt\", MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:569
msgid ""
"First, a detached bind-mount mount object of I</var> is created and "
"associated with the file descriptor I<srcfd>.  Then, the mount object is "
"attached to I</mnt> using B<move_mount>(2)  with B<\\"
"%MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH> to request that the detached mount object "
"associated with the file descriptor I<srcfd> be moved (and thus attached) to "
"I</mnt>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:577
#, no-wrap
msgid "mount(\"/var\", \"/mnt\", NULL, MS_BIND, NULL);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:586
msgid ""
"B<\\%OPEN_TREE_CLONE> can be combined with B<\\%AT_RECURSIVE> to create "
"recursive detached bind-mount mount objects, which in turn can be attached "
"to mount points to create recursive bind-mounts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:592
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int srcfd = open_tree(AT_FDCWD, \"/var\",\n"
"                      OPEN_TREE_CLONE | AT_RECURSIVE);\n"
"move_mount(srcfd, \"\", AT_FDCWD, \"/mnt\", MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:602
#, no-wrap
msgid "mount(\"/var\", \"/mnt\", NULL, MS_BIND | MS_REC, NULL);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:614
msgid ""
"One of the primary benefits of using B<open_tree>()  and B<move_mount>(2)  "
"over the traditional B<mount>(2)  is that operating with I<dirfd>-style file "
"descriptors is far easier and more intuitive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:619
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int srcfd = open_tree(100, \"\", AT_EMPTY_PATH | OPEN_TREE_CLONE);\n"
"move_mount(srcfd, \"\", 200, \"foo\", MOVE_MOUNT_F_EMPTY_PATH);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:631
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"mount(\"/proc/self/fd/100\",\n"
"      \"/proc/self/fd/200/foo\",\n"
"      NULL, MS_BIND, NULL);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:639
msgid ""
"In addition, you can use the file descriptor returned by B<open_tree>()  as "
"the I<dirfd> argument to any \"*at()\" system calls:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:650
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int dirfd, fd;\n"
"\\&\n"
"dirfd = open_tree(AT_FDCWD, \"/etc\", OPEN_TREE_CLONE);\n"
"fd = openat(dirfd, \"passwd\", O_RDONLY);\n"
"fchmodat(dirfd, \"shadow\", 0000, 0);\n"
"close(dirfd);\n"
"close(fd);\n"
"/* The bind-mount is now destroyed */\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:666
msgid ""
"The following is an example of how B<open_tree_attr>()  can be used to take "
"an existing id-mapped mount and construct a new bind-mount mount object with "
"a different B<\\%MOUNT_ATTR_IDMAP> attribute.  The resultant detached mount "
"object can be used like any other mount object returned by B<open_tree>()."
msgstr ""

#.  Using .attr_clr is not strictly necessary but makes the intent clearer.
#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:696
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int nsfd1, nsfd2;\n"
"int mntfd1, mntfd2, mntfd3;\n"
"struct mount_attr attr;\n"
"mntfd1 = open_tree(AT_FDCWD, \"/foo\", OPEN_TREE_CLONE);\n"
"\\&\n"
"/* Configure the id-mapping of mntfd1 */\n"
"nsfd1 = open(\"/proc/1234/ns/user\", O_RDONLY);\n"
"memset(&attr, 0, sizeof(attr));\n"
"attr.attr_set = MOUNT_ATTR_IDMAP;\n"
"attr.userns_fd = nsfd1;\n"
"mount_setattr(mntfd1, \"\", AT_EMPTY_PATH, &attr, sizeof(attr));\n"
"\\&\n"
"/* Create a new copy with a different id-mapping */\n"
"nsfd2 = open(\"/proc/5678/ns/user\", O_RDONLY);\n"
"memset(&attr, 0, sizeof(attr));\n"
"attr.attr_clr = MOUNT_ATTR_IDMAP;\n"
"attr.attr_set = MOUNT_ATTR_IDMAP;\n"
"attr.userns_fd = nsfd2;\n"
"mntfd2 = open_tree_attr(mntfd1, \"\", OPEN_TREE_CLONE,\n"
"                        &attr, sizeof(attr));\n"
"\\&\n"
"/* Create a new copy with the id-mapping cleared */\n"
"memset(&attr, 0, sizeof(attr));\n"
"attr.attr_clr = MOUNT_ATTR_IDMAP;\n"
"mntfd3 = open_tree_attr(mntfd1, \"\", OPEN_TREE_CLONE,\n"
"                        &attr, sizeof(attr));\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/open_tree.2:703
msgid ""
"B<open_tree_attr>()  can also be used with attached mount objects; the above "
"example is only intended to be illustrative."
msgstr ""

