#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/statmount.2:85
msgid ""
"To access a mount's status, the caller must have CAP_SYS_ADMIN in the user "
"namespace.  In case of accessing a mount in a foreign mount namespace "
"(specified via I<req.mnt_ns_id> or I<req.mnt_ns_fd>), the foreign mount "
"namespace should be child of the current namespace."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/statmount.2:97
msgid ""
"This function returns information about a mount, storing it in the buffer "
"pointed to by I<smbuf>.  The returned buffer is a I<struct statmount> which "
"is of size I<bufsize> with the fields filled in as described below.  "
"I<flags> must either be 0 or B<STATMOUNT_BY_FD>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/statmount.2:99 build/C/man2/statx.2:100
msgid "(Note that reserved space and padding is omitted.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/statmount.2:106
msgid ""
"I<req.size> is used by the kernel to determine which I<struct\\~mnt_id_req> "
"is being passed in; it should always be set to "
"I<sizeof(struct\\~mnt_id_req)>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/statmount.2:116
msgid ""
"I<req.mnt_ns_fd> can be obtained from B<PIDFD_GET_MNT_NAMESPACE> "
"B<ioctl>(2)  operation or by opening a file descriptor to I</proc/>pidI</ns/"
"mnt> and is used to specify a foreign mount namespace in which to query "
"I<req.mnt_id> (since Linux 6.18)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/statmount.2:129
msgid ""
"I<req.mnt_fd> is a file descriptor on a mount.  If B<STATMOUNT_BY_FD> flag "
"is specified, I<req.mnt_id> and I<req.mnt_ns_id> are zeroed, the function "
"will return information about the mount the file descriptor is on (since "
"Linux 7.0)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/statmount.2:139
msgid ""
"The fd can also be on a mount that has been lazily unmounted (see "
"B<umount2>(2)  with B<MNT_DETACH>).  In this case, B<STATMOUNT_MNT_POINT> "
"and B<STATMOUNT_MNT_NS_ID> will be unset, since an unmounted mount is no "
"longer a part of the filesystem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man2/statmount.2:148
msgid ""
"I<req.mnt_id> can be obtained from either B<statx>(2)  using "
"B<STATX_MNT_ID_UNIQUE> or from B<listmount>(2)  and is used as the "
"identifier to query the status of the desired mount point."
msgstr ""

